WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.625
Windows, Linux, and macOS can all support local inference.

00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:07.680
The practical choice depends on hardware support, operator skill, application needs,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.191
security controls, automation, and the ability to maintain the environment.

00:00:11.191 --> 00:00:15.352
NVIDIA acceleration commonly relies on CUDA-compatible drivers and runtimes.

00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:19.610
AMD support may use ROCm or other compatible paths depending on hardware and operating

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:20.140
system.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.920
Vulkan can provide a cross-platform acceleration option for supported runtimes.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.695
Apple Silicon uses Metal and unified memory,

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:29.655
allowing CPU and GPU components to share a memory pool.

00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:33.345
Available capacity, bandwidth, thermals, and model support still set limits.

00:00:33.345 --> 00:00:36.160
Unified memory should not be treated as unlimited VRAM.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.720
Driver and runtime versions must align with the hardware, operating system,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.560
inference software, and libraries.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:46.455
A powerful GPU can perform poorly or fail to load a model when the acceleration stack is

00:00:46.455 --> 00:00:47.955
unsupported or inconsistent.

00:00:47.955 --> 00:00:50.080
Stability matters more than chasing every update.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.280
Maintain a known working configuration, record versions, review release changes,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.850
test upgrades, and preserve rollback options.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.120
Security updates and unsupported dependencies still need timely attention.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.855
The software environment is part of capacity planning.

00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:07.210
Background applications, display usage, antivirus or security scanning, containers,

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.575
virtual machines, and multiple runtimes can consume memory and complicate troubleshooting.

00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:13.200
Standardize before tuning.
